==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From the Icelandic verb ''[[kenna]]'' ("to [[teach]]").
===Noun===
'''kennari''' {{m}}

# [[teacher]]
#: ''Hún er [[góður]] '''kennari'''.''
#:: She is a [[good]] '''teacher'''.
#: ''[[Jónas]] er [[undarlegur]] '''kennari''', en samt [[skemmtilegur]].'
#:: Mister [[Jónas]] is an [[odd]] '''teacher''', but [[fun]] nevertheless.

====Usage notes====
*The term '''kennari''' is a unisex term and can refer to both male an female teachers. However the term ''[[kennslukona]]'' (literally "[[teach]]ing [[woman]]") is only used of women.

====Derived terms====
*[[kennarasleikja]]

